Orientation: You are at Griffin Museum of Photography — this opening stop is about the place itself.

Before we look at anything on the walls, here is the story of Griffin Museum of Photography in Winchester, Massachusetts itself — who created it, why it exists, and what it is known for. Arthur Griffin was an American photographer. Building on the legacy of our founder, Arthur Griffin, we cultivate opportunities to engage with and better understand our diverse world through the photographic arts. The Griffin Museum of Photography is a 501(c)3 nonprofit organization dedicated to the art of photography. Guided by our mission, the Griffin Museum is committed to embedding diversity, equity, accessibility, and inclusion across all aspects of our work—including our mindset, practices, outreach, programming, and exhibitions. Founded in 1992 as a private foundation, the Griffin Museum of Photography became a nonprofit public charity in 2000. This account is drawn from the museum's own pages on griffinmuseum.org and public reference sources.

